UNIQUE ID GENERATOR

Everytime something gets created, a message, a payment, an order it needs an id. 
Handling IDs gets hard when many machines are creating messges at the same time. 

Four requirements of IDs
1. unique
2. sorted by time 
3. fits in 64 bits (BIGINT)
4. gaps are fine (1001 -> 1005 -> 1008)

Method 1:
Ticket server (Flikkers): a table with single row, everytime someone needs an id, it adds 1 and return the id.

Every request has a round trip with ticket server which adds latency 
Single point of failure 
            (runs two 
                - one server only odd numbers, 
                - other only even
             But this is not sorted (lets say first message gtes 2 and next gets 1)
            )


Method 2:

UUID: You have to pick 1 billions of messages per second for 86 years for change of collission 50%.

It is 128 bits and completely random (not satisfying point 2 and 3)


Method 3:
Twitter's Snowflake:
Time + machine code + counter
First bit is always 0 so that number never goes negative 
41 bits goes to time it will take 69 years to exhaust
10 bits goes to machine code 
12 bits goes to the counter (It means, if one machine needs more than 2^12 (40896) ids in a sec, it has to wait)